WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.203
-So, I heard you talk about this
on "Howard Stern,"

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's really a cool story
which is that you became

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:11.878
pen pals with Donald Trump's
former lawyer, Michael Cohen

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to the point
that you actually

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.782 line:92%
went and visited him in prison

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:19.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I did, in federal prison
-So, how did it start?

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did the
pen-pal nature start?

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:25.191
-Well, you know, he sounds
like he's one of my brothers

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
Excuse me.
[ Sneezes ]

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.828 line:92%
No COVID. I swear, no COVID.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll give that again
in case you want to edit it.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
He sounds like he's somebody
from my neighborhood,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.367 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Michael Cohen.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, every time
I heard him talk, I'm like

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:36.870 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"What is he?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
From the next town over
on Long Island?"

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he seemed very familia
to me the whole time

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:45.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I knew of his existence
which was during

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
that whole period when Trump
was attacking me on,

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.349 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you know, a daily basis.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I knew, from knowing
a little about

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.387 size:81% position:41%
the Trump Organization
and how it all worked,

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.355 line:92%
that it was him who did it

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't Donald Trump
sitting there

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.793
calling David Pecker and,
you know, Donald Trump

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:03.596
making all the plans of how they
were going to best attack me

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew that it was him,
so I kind of looked at him

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:09.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
with fascination the whole tim
that I was involved

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.570 size:81% position:41% line:92%
in any way with Trump.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when
Trump got impeached,

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:13.473 line:92%
I kept thinking about him.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Imagine that
he gets impeached,

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.844
he's in The White House,
and the guy that told you

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:21.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do all this,
you're sitting in jail,

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's sitting in
The White House.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.349 size:75% position:38% line:92%
How does that feel?"

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I wrote him a letter
and I put a little picture

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
of myself with
my daughter in there,

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.122
'cause I didn't know if he'd
believe that it was me, right?

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.423 line:92%
It was a handwritten letter.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:34.427
And about a week later,
I get an e-mail from him.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I had no idea
that they were

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
allowed to use e-mail,
prisoners.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:39.599 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did you know that?

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.267 line:92%
-I wouldn't have known that.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.102 line:92%
-I didn't know that either

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:47.407
So, I was waiting for, you know,
mail delivered by the mailman,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.408 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and it was an e-mail.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"They're giving them e-mail?

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.213 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And he was very kind.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said that he was shocke
that I wrote him

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:58.718
and that he apologized and
he was sorry for what he did

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of people
had told him that I was

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
a good person,
and he felt so bad.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.325 line:92%
And, so, then I wrote him back

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we started sort of
writing, you know?

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
And after a few months
of that, he said,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Would you ever come
and visit me?

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.867 size:84% position:42%
I'd like to apologize
to your face, you know?

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:16.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd like to
talk to you one-on-one,"

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
which you really
can't do in a prison

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.272 line:92%
because there's so many people

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, I go there
and I get into this --

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
what looks like
a college campus.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it has no guard gates.
It has no towers.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.415 line:92%
-So he's in a very nice jail

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's in what I believe they
call Camp Cupcake.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I walked in,
and there he was.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he looked pretty good,
I have to say.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.491 line:92%
And we sat and we talked.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:41.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
And next to me was a guy,
friend of Michael's in prison.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "Oh, Rosie, don't
you remember me?"

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Give me a hint?"

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said,
"We sat next to each other

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:51.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
at Liza Minnelli's
60th birthday party."

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was like, "What?"

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.842 size:78% position:39%
And he was apparently
a friend of Liza's

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:58.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
who did some AIDS charity
and then got caught

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, you know, doing --
And he's been in there for -

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:05.084
Like, since that birthday party,
he's been in jail.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.653 line:92%
-So you knew multiple people

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you went to visit
Michael Cohen.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I knew that guy,
and then another guy

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:10.924 line:92%
came over to me and said,

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.893 size:81% position:41%
"My kid goes to school
with your daughter."

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic.
-I was like, "Wow."

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you --
Do you feel as though --

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.366 size:78% position:39%
You know, obviously,
he apologized to you,

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.100 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Michael Cohen.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
He seems like someone
who appreciates

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
what he did wrong
and, in general,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
seems to be trying to be
a better person.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:32.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that the bounce you got off
him when you spoke to him?

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's completely
what I got off him.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a great thing he told me
was that the whole time

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
he worked for Trump --
He had already made his mone

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
on his own, and the whole time
that he worked for Trump,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
his wife and kids kept saying,
"You got to quit that job.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to quit that job."
The whole time he worked there

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he got tears in his eyes
and he said,

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I just wish I'd listened
to my wife and kids.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
If I had listened to my
wife and kids,

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wouldn't be here
in this position, you know?"

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:55.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can imagine
when this is over,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:04:00.073
one of the first things you will
do is go see a Broadway show

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.040 line:92%
Is that is an accurate guess

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is totally accurate.
I can't wait.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's my big --
You know, I don't know

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
how long it's gonna take,
because those seats

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:07.880 size:84% position:42% line:92%
are so cramped together

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're a lot of money
for a ticket.

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm worried about what
the economy --

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.186 line:92%
all these unemployed people.

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to be a tough
road after we're out of this

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.358 size:78% position:39%
the viral part of it,
when we get back to

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:20.326 line:92%
the just living, you know?

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.061 line:92%
-You did a reboot of your show

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
to raise money
for The Actors Fund.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
You raised over a
half-a-million dollars.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.368 line:92%
That was an incredible gesture

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there a way for people,
if they want to

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:33.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
make a contribution to that,
to still do it now?

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.007 line:92%
-Yeah, The Actors Fund is great.

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:38.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
It serves all actors and peopl
in the industry of theater

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:41.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, you know,
stagehands from Minnesota

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.716 line:92%
or people in a touring company

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, and it really doesn'
just encompass actors,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:47.887 line:92%
because I had some people say,

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, you rich actors are takin
care of each other."

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, that's not what
The Actors Fund does.

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you can go to
theactorsfund.org

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
and look it up
and see what they do.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they have
a donate button there, too

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.433 line:92%
to help people get through this.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't wait to watch
on Sunday night.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.873
And it's always a pleasure
Rosie O'Donnell, everyone.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks, Seth.
Good to see you.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.209 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Alright, be well.

